+
+## Account settings and passkey service
+
+Account settings are available at `/devtools-times/account`. Sign-in saves the
+service's bearer `token` in tab-scoped session storage and opens this page.
+`PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_API_URL` can override the existing remote API base URL at build
+time. The configured service must allow the application's origin, Authorization
+header, and PATCH/DELETE requests through CORS.
+
+**Backend integration required:** the current remote service does not expose
+`GET /api/passkeys`. The UI reports this as unavailable. This repository does not
+contain the authentication backend or a WebAuthn credential database, and does not
+create substitute credentials or treat browser storage as a credential registry.
+The account service must implement the following authenticated contract:
+
+- `POST /login`: accepts `{ username, password }`, returns `{ token }`.
+- `GET /passkeys`: returns the complete snapshot below (never a paginated list).
+- `PATCH /passkeys/:credentialId`: accepts `{ displayName }` (trimmed, 1–100
+  characters). Updates the key's account nickname and returns a complete snapshot.
+- `DELETE /passkeys/:credentialId`: revokes the credential and returns a complete
+  snapshot **after** the deletion has committed, including an empty array if the
+  final credential was removed.
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "your-app.example",
+  "user": {
+    "id": "base64url-webauthn-user-handle",
+    "name": "reader@example.com",
+    "displayName": "Reader"
+  },
+  "passkeys": [
+    {
+      "id": "base64url-credential-id",
+      "displayName": "Personal laptop",
+      "createdAt": "2026-10-23T10:00:00Z",
+      "lastUsedAt": null
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+All passkey routes must verify the bearer session and scope access to its owner;
+never accept a client-selected user ID. Return 401 for expired sessions, enforce
+name validation on the server, and consider requiring recent authentication for
+revocation. Return `Cache-Control: no-store`. The RP ID and user handle must be the
+ones used at WebAuthn registration; the RP ID must be valid for the app's origin.
+
+Only successful, validated snapshots are passed to WebAuthn's
+`signalAllAcceptedCredentials` and `signalCurrentUserDetails`. The latter updates
+account identity metadata, not an individual key's nickname. Nicknames are saved
+in the account service. A failed or unsupported browser signal never rolls back a
+successful server mutation, and the UI offers retry/manual password-manager
+instructions. Provider behavior and user-customized names remain under the
+password manager's control. See the [WebAuthn Signal API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/webauthn-signal-api).
